WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.217
Professional sellers can add products to their Amazon inventory in bulk by uploading a spreadsheet

00:00:08.217 --> 00:00:09.860
or inventory file.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:16.951
Creating an inventory file takes time, but it can also save time later when you want to add or edit

00:00:16.951 --> 00:00:18.820
a large number of product listings.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:25.800
Alternatively, Amazon can also generate a template based on the product type that you select.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:32.055
Every product type has attributes that are specific and related to the product type, so it's important

00:00:32.055 --> 00:00:34.400
to choose the right one when listing.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:40.964
Use them to match your offers to existing listings or to create product detail pages and listings

00:00:40.964 --> 00:00:41.960
for new products.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:49.446
Remember that you must be a product's brand owner or a brand qualified seller to create a new detail

00:00:49.446 --> 00:00:52.320
page for an Amazon brand registry enrolled product.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.560
There are three basic steps in the bulk listing process.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.500
One, download a spreadsheet template.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.300
Two, add your product information.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.580
And three, upload your file to Seller Central.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:12.183
Once you've uploaded an inventory file, you can monitor its status and correct any errors that are

00:01:12.183 --> 00:01:12.540
identified.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:16.040
Let's start with creating your inventory file.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:22.974
You can access this option from the Seller Central main menu, hover over Catalog, then click Add

00:01:22.974 --> 00:01:23.400
Products.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.640
On the list your products page, click Spreadsheet.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:32.704
Under the Spreadsheet tab, click Download Blank Template and choose the template you need from the

00:01:32.704 --> 00:01:33.740
pop-up menu.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:38.660
Let's start with matching to products already sold in the Amazon store.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:45.260
Select Get Listing Loader in the list products already in Amazon's Catalog box.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.560
A pop-up box will appear.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:56.020
Select the spreadsheet language and add either the products ASIN, UPC, EAN, or GTIN into the box.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:01.720
You can search up to 500 product IDs to generate a pre-filled spreadsheet.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:06.700
Once you've added all the product IDs, select Generate Spreadsheet.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.280
To check the status of your file, click on View Previously Generated Templates.

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:15.560
Once your file is ready, you'll see a download button.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.140
Click on this button to access your spreadsheet.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:23.829
Start by saving the file as a text-tab-delimited file or .

00:02:23.829 --> 00:02:24.240
txt.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:31.240
Using this file format will help reduce the chances of your file having errors and being rejected.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:36.880
Consider adding a date to the file name to keep a record of your work on your local computer.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:41.640
When you open your inventory file template, you'll see multiple tabs.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.600
You'll add product information to the template tab.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:49.900
The Instructions tab provides guidance on filling in the template.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:54.340
The Data Definitions tab explains the meaning of each attribute.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:03:00.300
And the Valid Values tab provides guidance on the accepted values for each attribute.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:05.627
It's important that you review all the tabs and read through them carefully

00:03:05.627 --> 00:03:08.540
before you start making changes on the template tab.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:13.400
Select the template tab and fill out all the information for your offer.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:17.380
Anything that has a gray box doesn't need to be filled out.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:23.360
We recommend filling out as many details as possible, but only those with a red box are required.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:28.640
Once you've entered all the information, save your file on your local computer.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:32.880
Later in this training, we walk you through the steps to upload your spreadsheet.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:37.760
Now, let's review how to create new product listings in bulk.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:44.011
Select Download Product Spreadsheet in the list products that are not currently in Amazon's catalog

00:03:44.011 --> 00:03:44.380
box.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:48.600
First, you'll search and select the product types you want to list.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:55.447
You can use the Search tool, which allows you to identify and select product categories, also called

00:03:55.447 --> 00:03:56.180
Product Types.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:03.060
The selections you make add relevant product attribute columns to your inventory file template.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:10.911
For example, if you select the product category digital cameras, columns for video capture, resolution,

00:04:10.911 --> 00:04:13.700
and audio encoding language will appear.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:20.520
If you want to search for product categories, enter your product name or a descriptor in the search

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.420
bar and press the Search button.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:27.620
For example, you might search for shoes, basketball, or kids' toys.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:31.460
The Search tool will list all related product types.

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:37.540
Browse carefully and click the Select button next to the product type that matches your product.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:41.940
Each selection you make will appear to the right of the search results.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:46.020
You can click the X next to a selection to remove a category.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:52.420
You can also select Browse via product category to manually browse the different product categories.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:57.300
Locate the overarching category for a product from the list.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.820
Then select each subcategory to narrow the results.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:07.220
For example, you might select Clothing Shoes and Jewelry, then Men, Watches, and Watch Bands.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:13.273
Click the Select button next to the subcategory that matches your product, which will add it to

00:05:13.273 --> 00:05:15.140
the list below for your file template.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:19.860
You might see a Lock and Request Approval button next to some product types.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:26.260
That means you need to obtain approval from Amazon before listing products in that category.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:32.100
Click the Request Approval button, which will take you to our Categories and Products Requiring

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.300
Approval Help page for step-by-step instructions.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:41.357
After selecting the product categories you want added to your spreadsheet, you'll select the stores

00:05:41.357 --> 00:05:43.460
where you want to create offers.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:48.820
When you're done, click Generate Spreadsheet to download your inventory file template.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:53.540
Once you've created your template, you'll add your product information.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:58.980
Start by saving the template as a text, tab-delimited file or .

00:05:58.980 --> 00:05:59.380
txt.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.500
Be sure to add a date to the file name to keep a record of your work.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.980
You'll want to use the most recently downloaded version of the template for product types.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:16.180
Amazon frequently updates templates and old versions may be incompatible and could result in errors.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:21.460
Be sure to enable editing on the spreadsheet before making any revisions.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:25.060
If you don't enable this feature, you won't be able to save your changes.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:29.540
When you open your spreadsheet, you'll see multiple tabs.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:32.740
You'll add product information to the template tab.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:41.740
The instructions, images, example, data definitions, browse data and valid values tabs provide information

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:42.740
and guidance.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:49.780
Start by reviewing the Instructions tab, which explains in detail how to use the template.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:55.380
It's worth reading this all the way through, especially the first time you create an inventory file.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:00.020
The Images tab outlines Amazon's image requirements.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:04.233
If you're including images for a new product or if you're recommending

00:07:04.233 --> 00:07:08.580
updated images for an existing product, review this tab for important guidance.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:13.780
The Example tab provides several sample product rows for your reference.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:19.700
Take a look if you'd like to see in detail how your inventory file should look when it's completed.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:25.620
The Data Definitions tab defines each attribute within your inventory file.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:30.420
If you're unsure how to complete an attribute column or whether it's required,

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:37.420
refer to this tab for definitions and use, accepted values, an example of each attribute, as well

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:39.460
as the required or optional indicator.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:45.540
The Browse Data tab shows how your products will be found by customers browsing the Amazon store.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:52.415
Finally, the Valid Values tab provides a list of acceptable terms for certain product attribute

00:07:52.415 --> 00:07:52.820
columns.

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:59.215
If you're unsure about an entry for a specific attribute, consult this table and select a value

00:07:59.215 --> 00:08:01.860
that appears in a corresponding row and column.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:07.380
Back on the Template tab, each row represents a single product.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:14.291
Use one row to match your offer to an existing listing or to create a product detail page and offer

00:08:14.291 --> 00:08:15.620
for a new product.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:19.700
Each column represents a single product attribute.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:25.780
There are hidden columns in the spreadsheet that can be unhidden by either clicking the "2" button

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:32.468
in the top left corner to unhide all columns or by clicking the plus button to unhide all columns

00:08:32.468 --> 00:08:32.820
individually.

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:38.740
Start entering a product's information using the drop-down in column A for product type.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:44.527
Once you've made your selection, all the other required entries for the row will be outlined in

00:08:44.527 --> 00:08:44.820
red.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:50.980
If your template includes more than one product type, show multiple all entries for other product

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:54.980
categories will be grayed out to indicate that they shouldn't be completed.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:09:00.580
You'll type many entries manually, but some will have a drop-down like column A.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:06.660
Make sure you don't edit any information in the first three rows highlighted in various colors.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.020
Doing so will cause errors during upload.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:17.454
Fill in each required entry in red which will include the seller SKU, your stock keeping unit or

00:09:17.454 --> 00:09:24.884
personal seller identifier, and the external product ID, which will be the ASIN or a GTIN, like

00:09:24.884 --> 00:09:27.540
a UPC, ISBN, EAN, or JAN.

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:33.860
The Record Action column is an important field in the spreadsheet because it will dictate whether

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:37.780
you're making a change to every attribute or just some attributes.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:45.007
In some templates, the column is titled Record Action and in other templates, the column is titled

00:09:45.007 --> 00:09:45.780
Update Delete.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:49.780
This column is used to make changes to all ASINs.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:55.220
The Partial Update column is used to update only specific attributes that have been entered.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:04.047
Your price is also a required field, even if it's zero for a business-only offer or an item that

00:10:04.047 --> 00:10:05.220
is out of stock.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:11.140
Next, fill in any unoutlined entries for optional attributes that you want to complete.

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:19.229
After the required columns in red, you'll find Variation column, an Image column, and a choice to

00:10:19.229 --> 00:10:22.100
choose either parent or child under Variation.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:28.153
For example, let's say you want to sell a women's shirt that comes in two different sizes, small

00:10:28.153 --> 00:10:28.900
and large.

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:32.740
Maybe it also comes in two colors, yellow and blue.

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:36.180
You'll want to start adding information with the parent item.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:43.645
The parent is a non-buyable, non-physical product and is only used to drive product searches and

00:10:43.645 --> 00:10:45.380
relate buyable child products.

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:50.900
This means you only need to complete required columns for the parent items that fulfill these functions.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:57.380
In this example, outer material type is also required due to the product category.

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:06.900
These will always include the seller SKU, brand, product ID, product type, title, item type, main

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:07.700
image URL.

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:14.740
For the child products, you'll need to complete all required attribute columns as you would for

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:15.940
any other buyable product.

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:21.140
Some of these columns will be identical across a set of child products.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:27.300
The entry for brand must be the same for each child SKU to prevent submission errors.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:34.460
Other attribute columns require unique entries for each product variation because they are different

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.860
for each child item.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:38.260
For example, different sizes or colors.

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:46.660
These always include the seller SKU, title which should include variation information like size

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.660
and color, and product ID.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:55.960
Your varying attributes, your price and main image URL could be the same or different according

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:58.340
to the properties of each child product.

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:04.150
After entering the required information for your parent and child products, you'll need to enter

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:09.620
four additional attributes in your spreadsheet to establish the parent child relationship.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:13.620
This information links your listings in the Amazon store.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:17.460
Get started by scrolling over to the variation column.

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:23.932
In this column, choose parent for your parent item and child for each child item using the drop

00:12:23.932 --> 00:12:24.260
down.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:30.820
Copy the parent SKU from column B into the variation section in the column parent SKU.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.180
Leave this column blank for the parent item.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:40.260
You'll also find columns related to the discovery of products in the Amazon store in green.

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:44.980
Light green product enrichment columns for extra product information.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:50.260
Yellow dimensions columns and red fulfillment columns for shipping information.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:57.264
At the end of the spreadsheet, you'll find purple compliance columns, pink and burgundy offer columns

00:12:57.264 --> 00:12:59.620
for pricing and other listing information.

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:05.620
And Jade B2B columns for sellers listing product for Amazon business customers.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:11.460
You'll want to leave column quantity US as zero until you're ready to launch.

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:14.660
This way your product won't go live before you're ready to list.

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:18.500
You'll also find variation options in teal.

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:22.500
Some sellers fill out every attribute column.

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.740
Some fill out only required columns.

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:31.540
In general, the more data you provide, the more information and options customers have while making

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:32.420
purchasing decisions.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:38.340
Remember that once you've completed a row for a product, you can keep a saved copy of your file

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:42.580
to make quick and easy edits to your product and listing information later.

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:47.700
However, it's not recommended to use templates that are more than 90 days old.

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:52.580
Instead, download the latest templates to avoid submission errors.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:58.660
When you finish adding products to your inventory file template, make sure you save your changes

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:00.420
and keep a copy for your records.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:05.620
Then you're ready for the third and final step, uploading your file to Seller Central.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:09.460
Under the spreadsheet tab, select upload file.

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:14.900
Drag and drop your file or click browse files to search for and select your file.

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:19.780
Once your file is validated, the submit products button will activate.

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:25.609
If your file type isn't recognized, a drop-down will appear instead and you'll be able to select

00:14:25.609 --> 00:14:26.580
your file type.

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:32.928
Before uploading, you can select receive email notifications about this feed if you'd like to be

00:14:32.928 --> 00:14:35.460
notified when your file is done processing.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:38.820
When you're ready, click the submit products button.

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:43.620
If you're only uploading information for a few products, it will take a few minutes to process.

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:46.740
Larger uploads can take several hours.

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:52.980
Your inventory will be available for purchase in the Amazon store once the upload is complete.

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:58.500
You can check the status of an upload by clicking check upload status under the spreadsheet tab,

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:06.028
which lists the date, time, batch ID, status and a link to the processing report for your most recent

00:15:06.028 --> 00:15:06.820
completed uploads.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:10.580
Check your processing report to address any errors.

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:16.740
You'll use this process to match offers to existing listings and you'll use it to create product

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:18.820
detail pages and listings for new products.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:24.340
You can use a single inventory file to both match and create listings.

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:32.180
If your file includes a product ID or GTIN for an item and a matching ID exists in the Amazon store,

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:36.180
we'll match your offer to the existing product detail page.

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:41.502
We'll also attempt to match a product by manufacturer or other information if you don't include

00:15:41.502 --> 00:15:42.500
a product ID.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:49.003
If we can't match a product to an existing product in the Amazon store, we'll create a new product

00:15:49.003 --> 00:15:49.620
detail page.

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:56.340
After adding product listings to your inventory, you can use the same process to make edits to listings

00:15:56.340 --> 00:15:59.620
or to suggest changes to product detail pages in bulk.

00:16:00.740 --> 00:16:06.165
Start by going back to your saved inventory file and for faster processing, remove any products

00:16:06.165 --> 00:16:09.300
you don't want to adjust, then save the new copy.

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:15.988
If you just want to edit an offer, update your price, quantity, business price, or any other offer-

00:16:15.988 --> 00:16:21.140
related information in your inventory file, you can leave all other entries the same.

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:27.220
Note that if you delete an offer-related entry, it will register as a zero on Seller Central.

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:32.820
For example, deleting a price for a product will set the price at $0.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:38.793
If you're a qualified seller and want to suggest changes to your product detail page, make the suggested

00:16:38.793 --> 00:16:41.300
updates in the relevant attribute column.

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:45.460
After making edits to your inventory file, you can upload it normally.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:49.300
You'll see the offer updates within 15 minutes of your upload.

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:55.380
We'll also review suggested product changes and make any updates within 24 hours.

00:16:55.940 --> 00:17:01.924
If for any reason you want to replace your entire inventory in the Amazon Store, there is also an

00:17:01.924 --> 00:17:05.620
option under the spreadsheet tab to purge and replace your inventory.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:11.380
You'll click the link to select this option, then upload your inventory file normally.

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:17.492
Keep in mind that this will delete all your current listings in the Amazon Store, including any

00:17:17.492 --> 00:17:20.180
products not in the file you're currently uploading.

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:25.860
It will replace your entire inventory with the products in your new file only.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:32.676
Matching and creating product listings in bulk might seem daunting at first, but the extra effort

00:17:32.676 --> 00:17:36.020
can save you time, energy, and effort in the long run.

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:40.340
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
